  "version": 1,
  "title": "Exact LRX diameter of the symmetric group",
  "abstract": "For every n >= 4 the Cayley graph of S_n with unit-cost generators L = (0 1 ... n-1), R = L inverse, and X = (0 1) has diameter n*(n-1)/2. The formalization proves upper and lower bounds and a literal L/R/X word of at most that length between every ordered pair of permutations. The independent Challenge defines the moves, their word evaluation, and the undirected Cayley graph using Mathlib alone.",
